(3866923, 543806, 14386, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by smyk:</b></div><hr/><i> HAHAHA, "after yours" you said. It''s literally after his! Very different shot compared to your your other work. Good work. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Right on Christophe.:)  All credit goes to Pedro and shecoya.  I would have loved this to ribbon just for that purpose.:)</td>', 'Originally posted by smyk: HAHAHA, "after yours" you said. It''s literally after his! Very different shot compared to your your other work. Good work.   Right on Christophe.:)  All credit goes to Pedro and shecoya.  I would have loved this to ribbon just for that purpose.:)', '2007-07-04 10:58:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(3867008, 543365, 54446, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Art Roflmao:</b></div><hr/><i> I know nothing about these (or any other) animals, but it is interesting that the young ones of this species have Nerf horns until they are old enough to get the real, sharp ones. ;-)<br/> <br/>Congrats on an incredible capture and a top 10 placement! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Actually, not horns at all.  Those are antlers, which are re-grown each year and shed each year, in total.  You are confused with other species, such as bighorn sheep or mountain goats, which do have horns.... that grow incrementally each year.<br/> <br/>Only the male wapiti have antlers.  Antler growth is minimal until the animals are a few years of age.</td>', 'Originally posted by Art Roflmao: I know nothing about these (or any other) animals, but it is interesting that the young ones of this species have Nerf horns until they are old enough to get the real, sharp ones. ;-) Congrats on an incredible capture and a top 10 placement!   Actually, not horns at all.  Those are antlers, which are re-grown each year and shed each year, in total.  You are confused with other species, such as bighorn sheep or mountain goats, which do have horns.... that grow incrementally each year. Only the male wapiti have antlers.  Antler growth is minimal until the animals are a few years of age.', '2007-07-04 11:17:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(3867032, 543975, 66384, '<td valign="top">This is very surreal to me. The processing makes her face look quite old, while her body and hands look so young. It gives an interesting dreamlike twist to a girl doing something she isn''t old enough to do. And the fact that it isn''t really a car tops it all off. <br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-07-04 10:25:28.</i></td>', 'This is very surreal to me. The processing makes her face look quite old, while her body and hands look so young. It gives an interesting dreamlike twist to a girl doing something she isn''t old enough to do. And the fact that it isn''t really a car tops it all off. ', '2007-07-04 11:23:44.000000', '2007-07-04 11:25:28.000000', 0),
(3867066, 543637, 24454, '<td valign="top">Awww. .this is beautiful!   A perfect depiction of solo!  Jonathan Livingston never looked so beautiful and solitary :)<br/> <br/></td>', 'Awww. .this is beautiful!   A perfect depiction of solo!  Jonathan Livingston never looked so beautiful and solitary :) ', '2007-07-04 11:35:05.000000', NULL, 0),
