(3888141, 543917, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>"Solo to the Ground ..." is a good entry into the Solo Challenge.  Oh I am so excited that I got one of your image, especially one from the Angel series.  <br/> <br/>I really like the black and white choice, it really draws out our subject.  The placement of the subject is good.  I really like the image.  It just feels like their might be something missing but I really can''t put my finger on it, but then again maybe that is the point.  <br/> <br/>I really hope this challenge has inspired you hop back into swing of things so that we can see more of your creative shots! <br/> <br/></td>', '*Critique Club* "Solo to the Ground ..." is a good entry into the Solo Challenge.  Oh I am so excited that I got one of your image, especially one from the Angel series.   I really like the black and white choice, it really draws out our subject.  The placement of the subject is good.  I really like the image.  It just feels like their might be something missing but I really can''t put my finger on it, but then again maybe that is the point.   I really hope this challenge has inspired you hop back into swing of things so that we can see more of your creative shots!  ', '2007-07-10 04:18:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(3888145, 541663, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>"Lone Flame" is a strong entry into the Solo Challenge.  <br/> <br/>You have really nailed the subject, this almost looks like it could be a greeting cards (a serious one).<br/> <br/>The composition is very strong and instantly grabs the viewers eye.  I really like how smooth the black is,  we don''t see any spots or pixels.  Honestly I am not sure what I could say to make this image score higher.  Maybe a little more of the candle but we might loose the perspective. <br/> <br/>I really can tell you are excellent with light and lighting your subject in this piece as well as others you have previously entered.  I really look forward to more of your photos.</td>', '*Critique Club* "Lone Flame" is a strong entry into the Solo Challenge.   You have really nailed the subject, this almost looks like it could be a greeting cards (a serious one). The composition is very strong and instantly grabs the viewers eye.  I really like how smooth the black is,  we don''t see any spots or pixels.  Honestly I am not sure what I could say to make this image score higher.  Maybe a little more of the candle but we might loose the perspective.  I really can tell you are excellent with light and lighting your subject in this piece as well as others you have previously entered.  I really look forward to more of your photos.', '2007-07-10 04:26:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(3888148, 543986, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>"Lonely....waiting for you" is a nice entry into the Solo Challenge.  <br/> <br/>I think you have a nice original concept here,  I like that you were brave and used an unusual angle for this piece.  <br/> <br/>Since this is a solo challenge I think the image may have scored higher if we didn''t have the side distractions like the vent and the pattern on the chair taking our eyes off the subject.  I really do like the side lighting  as well as the focus on her.  <br/> <br/>Overall very cool idea and nice use of lighting to draw us into the piece.  I look forward to seeing more of your work.</td>', '*Critique Club* "Lonely....waiting for you" is a nice entry into the Solo Challenge.   I think you have a nice original concept here,  I like that you were brave and used an unusual angle for this piece.   Since this is a solo challenge I think the image may have scored higher if we didn''t have the side distractions like the vent and the pattern on the chair taking our eyes off the subject.  I really do like the side lighting  as well as the focus on her.   Overall very cool idea and nice use of lighting to draw us into the piece.  I look forward to seeing more of your work.', '2007-07-10 04:30:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(3888151, 543113, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>"Urban nocturne" is a very awesome piece for the Solo challenge, especially since you were out shooting ant 2 am. <br/> <br/>What a nice opportunity you had with this piece.  Everything is this shot is just nice.  To start with the lighting really brings our eyes onto the subject.  Our subject is nice, I like the we have a back and side view of the musician. <br/> <br/>I also really like that you were able to include the audience in a natural setting.  Overall this is an awesome piece.  The only thing I really could say is that I would be curious to see if you cropped out a little more on the right hand side to put our subject more on the third line of the frame and cut out some of the electronics.</td>', '*Critique Club* "Urban nocturne" is a very awesome piece for the Solo challenge, especially since you were out shooting ant 2 am.  What a nice opportunity you had with this piece.  Everything is this shot is just nice.  To start with the lighting really brings our eyes onto the subject.  Our subject is nice, I like the we have a back and side view of the musician.  I also really like that you were able to include the audience in a natural setting.  Overall this is an awesome piece.  The only thing I really could say is that I would be curious to see if you cropped out a little more on the right hand side to put our subject more on the third line of the frame and cut out some of the electronics.', '2007-07-10 04:37:41.000000', NULL, 0),
