(3948412, 544053, 30982, '<td valign="top">This is marvelous!  What a poignant and sweet shot.  I love the crop/composition and the very simple post processing - it keeps it clean and real.</td>', 'This is marvelous!  What a poignant and sweet shot.  I love the crop/composition and the very simple post processing - it keeps it clean and real.', '2007-07-30 02:55:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(3948424, 544266, 30982, '<td valign="top">A lovely, rich quiet photograph - I''m very surprised this didn''t score higher, to tell you the truth.  It''s very well composed (though some may want the neck of the guitar - I don''t mind it missing), well exposed, and just an all around good picture well suited to the challenge.  I especially like the guitars in the background over his shoulder.  Nicely done!</td>', 'A lovely, rich quiet photograph - I''m very surprised this didn''t score higher, to tell you the truth.  It''s very well composed (though some may want the neck of the guitar - I don''t mind it missing), well exposed, and just an all around good picture well suited to the challenge.  I especially like the guitars in the background over his shoulder.  Nicely done!', '2007-07-30 02:59:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(3948799, 540777, 30982, '<td valign="top">I like it just the way it is.  I''m not sure where the flare comes from the lights, but I like it.  And the sky looks wonderfully smooth on this monitor - no complaints at all.  What''s most pleasing to me, other than the concept, which I very much like (I travel alone, though usually with a suitcase rather than a pack), is the sweeping curve created by both the woman and the land shape.  Great composition!</td>', 'I like it just the way it is.  I''m not sure where the flare comes from the lights, but I like it.  And the sky looks wonderfully smooth on this monitor - no complaints at all.  What''s most pleasing to me, other than the concept, which I very much like (I travel alone, though usually with a suitcase rather than a pack), is the sweeping curve created by both the woman and the land shape.  Great composition!', '2007-07-30 06:22:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(3966224, 543908, 53278, '<td valign="top">the yellow cast , the oversharpening, and the negative space, are what killed the image.<br/> <br/>this should have done better with a tigheter crop , and cooler colors.</td>', 'the yellow cast , the oversharpening, and the negative space, are what killed the image. this should have done better with a tigheter crop , and cooler colors.', '2007-08-03 15:29:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(3970036, 542427, 75478, '<td valign="top">ya thats a great shot.. shoulda scored higher..<br/>awesome shot..<br/> <br/>representin pentax!!!<br/>i have that exact camera set up.. with the 18-50/2.8 n the K10.. havent done too much macro with it though.. <br/> <br/>great shot mang<br/> <br/>Fav..</td>', 'ya thats a great shot.. shoulda scored higher..awesome shot.. representin pentax!!!i have that exact camera set up.. with the 18-50/2.8 n the K10.. havent done too much macro with it though..  great shot mang Fav..', '2007-08-05 04:16:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(3970222, 542427, 74979, '<td valign="top"><i>STILL an incredible image</i>!!</td>', 'STILL an incredible image!!', '2007-08-05 08:55:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(3974315, 544267, 19831, '<td valign="top">Actually, I think the wb is not a big factor. For me anyway, when I see a shot of performers, I know they are on stage, with stage lighting, I at least expect to see the effects of that live lighting. I see more weakness in the framing of the shot, honestly. The framing feels ''uncomfortable''. It''s not a head shot, it''s not a half or 3/4 shot. His arm is cut off on the bottom of the frame, and the guitar is not prominent. I''m left really wishing I could see more of the performer, adding context to the scene. Especially in a ''Solo'' theme of the shot, I''d like to see that he is jamming out a solo, if you know what I mean. Also, a minor thing, but the angle has the line of lights running through his head, a little bit of an awkward compositional feeling.</td>', 'Actually, I think the wb is not a big factor. For me anyway, when I see a shot of performers, I know they are on stage, with stage lighting, I at least expect to see the effects of that live lighting. I see more weakness in the framing of the shot, honestly. The framing feels ''uncomfortable''. It''s not a head shot, it''s not a half or 3/4 shot. His arm is cut off on the bottom of the frame, and the guitar is not prominent. I''m left really wishing I could see more of the performer, adding context to the scene. Especially in a ''Solo'' theme of the shot, I''d like to see that he is jamming out a solo, if you know what I mean. Also, a minor thing, but the angle has the line of lights running through his head, a little bit of an awkward compositional feeling.', '2007-08-06 15:02:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(3985393, 544234, 20530, '<td valign="top">WOW, I can''t believe I never saw this one! Amazing! This deserves a much higher score and many more comments. If I were to offer any improvement, it might be to crop a little more off the left side. The color, sharpness, DOF, detail...everything is so good. Just gorgeous!</td>', 'WOW, I can''t believe I never saw this one! Amazing! This deserves a much higher score and many more comments. If I were to offer any improvement, it might be to crop a little more off the left side. The color, sharpness, DOF, detail...everything is so good. Just gorgeous!', '2007-08-09 23:19:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(3987001, 544234, 67579, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by rox_rox:</b></div><hr/><i> WOW, I can''t believe I never saw this one! Amazing! This deserves a much higher score and many more comments. If I were to offer any improvement, it might be to crop a little more off the left side. The color, sharpness, DOF, detail...everything is so good. Just gorgeous! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>you are too kind Roxanne ;)</td>', 'Originally posted by rox_rox: WOW, I can''t believe I never saw this one! Amazing! This deserves a much higher score and many more comments. If I were to offer any improvement, it might be to crop a little more off the left side. The color, sharpness, DOF, detail...everything is so good. Just gorgeous!   you are too kind Roxanne ;)', '2007-08-10 14:06:33.000000', NULL, 0),
