(4365231, 544231, 14986, '<td valign="top">This is YOUR kind of shot...tells a story, excellently done and makes me wonder about the subject.  You were robbed in this challenge.  Even if it didn''t ribbon it should have placed much, much higher.  <br/> <br/>What''s really nice here is the almost voyeristic angle, amazing that the lights are not blown out but you can still see he features cleanly, the really nice depth of field (getting the "laundry" not too blurry while having great focus on him...and that''s just the technical side.  Well done.</td>', 'This is YOUR kind of shot...tells a story, excellently done and makes me wonder about the subject.  You were robbed in this challenge.  Even if it didn''t ribbon it should have placed much, much higher.   What''s really nice here is the almost voyeristic angle, amazing that the lights are not blown out but you can still see he features cleanly, the really nice depth of field (getting the "laundry" not too blurry while having great focus on him...and that''s just the technical side.  Well done.', '2008-01-06 04:21:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(4393316, 540777, 53572, '<td valign="top">a very nice shot, indeed.  the flare may come from a bit of grub on the lens - something that wouldn''t make a difference except on bright points of light in the dark, where there''s no ambient light to absorb the flares.<br/> <br/>on another point - travelling solo is wonderful; i agree completely.  if you haven''t read it, ''<a href="//www.amazon.co.uk/Blessings-Good-Thick-Skirt-Travellers/dp/0006547486" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">the blessings of a good thick skirt</a>'' is a super book about female travellers. i''d really recommend it.  the title comes from an entry in the diary of a victorian adventurer.  she fell into a lion trap - the pit kind with spikes poking up - somewhere in africa.  however, her thick skirts and crinolines protected her from the spikes, and her porters came and pulled her out...</td>', 'a very nice shot, indeed.  the flare may come from a bit of grub on the lens - something that wouldn''t make a difference except on bright points of light in the dark, where there''s no ambient light to absorb the flares. on another point - travelling solo is wonderful; i agree completely.  if you haven''t read it, ''the blessings of a good thick skirt'' is a super book about female travellers. i''d really recommend it.  the title comes from an entry in the diary of a victorian adventurer.  she fell into a lion trap - the pit kind with spikes poking up - somewhere in africa.  however, her thick skirts and crinolines protected her from the spikes, and her porters came and pulled her out...', '2008-01-15 08:14:10.000000', NULL, 0),
